ly infeasible\n\nRequires creating playbooks per class, two-day design phase annotation, YAML spec auto-generates code. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Might need effort to create playbooks initially. So 3.\n\nNow produce output with evidence sentence then score.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON-like? The instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale in order give ... Probably just lines.\n\nI'll output:\n\nid: P2712\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The playbooks add templated schemas and auto-generated validation but keep compliance as a separate logging practice rather than redefining R&D-compliance relations. -> score 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Using per-class design playbooks to pre-map Article 12 events is a recognizable process improvement rather than an ingenious or surprising invention. -> score 2? Could be 3. Let's choose 2.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: By bounding the 'what to log' decision and generating schema validation, it materially reduces ad-hoc design time and improves traceability for high-risk systems. -> score 3? Could be 4. Hmm \"reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\" - does it solve? It decides what to log but doesn't implement logging itself. Might be partial. I'll give 3.\n\napplicability_evidence: The playbooks directly target the mandate to define loggable events under Article 12(2)(a)-(c) for each high-risk system class. -> score 4\n\nacceptability_evidence: Standardizing documentation and schema generation is a conventional engineering practice that raises no legal, social or political concerns. -> score 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Creating initial playbooks and integrating YAML-to-schema generation requires modest process change and tooling that is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab. -> score 3\n\nReturn.\n\n",
