nious/imaginative/surprising. 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common mundane boring.\n\nIs embedding logging in core architecture original? For AI labs facing EU AI Act, this is fairly standard \"shift-left compliance\". Probably common/mundane. Many suggest build logging in early. Might be common. Could be 1 = common, mundane, boring. Or 2 = interesting.\n\nReference class: set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to mandate. Expecting bake-in logging is expected. So originality low. Probably 1.\n\nEvidence: Building logging into design at the architecture stage is a common compliance engineering recommendation.\n\nScore 1.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm, anchored to this problem. 4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance). 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged.\n\nProposal bakes logging into core architecture with SDK and compliance engineer sign-off. That introduces new tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. Does it change relationship? It makes logging structural not cosmetic. Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. So level 2.\n\nEvidence: The proposal adds an SDK and review gates but keeps compliance framed as traceability/logging rather than redefining R&D.\n\nScore 2.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly. Provide fields.\n\nNeed format: maybe JSON? Instruction say