        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\nApply published anchored levels exactly, one level per subscale, and give one sentence evidence.\n\nProposal P1028: Automated Post-Market Monitoring Pipeline for Deployed Systems. Always-on infrastructure layer ingests automatic event logs mandated by Article12(1), correlates against predefined risk thresholds, flags anomalies relevant to safety incidents under Articles 79 and 72. Build dedicated observability service on existing MLOps tooling... Demonstrating active post-market monitoring is both legal duty and differentiator...\n\nRate subscales:\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nStated problem: AI R&D lab subject to regulation must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore...\n\nIdea is automated pipeline ingesting logs mandated by Article12(1) correlates etc. That directly applies to meeting logging mandate and post-market monitoring. Solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem). So applicability =4.\n\nEvidence sentence: The pipeline directly uses the Article 12(1) logs to meet traceability and monitoring obligations.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? It addresses logging mandate and post-market monitoring. It may be partial? Logging mandate is automatic recording; pipeline goes beyond just recording to monitoring. Might solve main problem of meeting logging mandate and adapting R&D. Probably reasonable and will contribute to solution? Does it solve the stated problem of how to meet logging mandate? Ingesting logs is needed but pipeline adds analysis. The core mandate is technically allow automatic recording. Pipeline assumes logs