ddresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice\n\nProposal creates community open standard extending requirements, positioning lab as setting research infrastructure standards rather than merely meeting them. That's change relationship between R&D and compliance obligations - logging woven into science, new partners. Might be paradigm stretching (3). Or paradigm breaking? Introduces new elements AND changes relationship... It does change relationship: from compliance burden to scientific leadership. Could be 4? Paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship... or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. This seems like paradigm stretching not breaking? Hmm. \"setting research infrastructure standards rather than merely meeting them\" suggests changing relationship. Maybe 3. Might be 4 because introduces new elements and changes relationship. The definition for 4 includes introduces new elements AND changes the relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. That fits. Could be 4.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree not only rare but also ingenious.\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious imaginative surprising\n3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane boring\n\nOpen research-grade logging schema for field, community standard extending Article 12. Is this unusual? Probably unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. Could be 3. Not necessarily never expressed before? Maybe similar ideas exist. I'd rate 3.\n\nLet's output JSON with evidence and scores.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give