g; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane\n\nEvent-logging SDK in starter templates. Is that common? Many labs use logging SDKs. Wrapping telemetry into zero-config decorators for compliance... Might be interesting but not ingenious. Probably 2 = interesting. Could be 3 unusual? Hmm. Common practice to have starter templates with logging. Might be common, mundane. I'd say 2 = interesting.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial)\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely\n1 = solves unrelated\n\nWill logging SDK solve mandate? It provides automatic recording of events, start/end timestamps, input data references, state snapshots. Article 12 requires logs for high-risk AI systems: period of each use, reference database, input data for match, identification of natural persons. Proposal covers start/end timestamps, input-data references, state snapshots. May not cover all requirements like identification of natural persons involved in verification. But it contributes. It will solve logging mandate for prototyping. Probably reasonable and will solve stated problem? Might be partial because only for prototypes from starter templates. Might be 3 = contribute.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation\n1 = intervention not stated\n\nDirectly applies: how to meet logging mandate and adapt R&D. Yes 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy low cost or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, reasonably feasible\n2 = significant change expensive/difficult but not impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nTwo engineers refactor internal monitoring middleware into pip package, make hard dependency in starter templates. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Two engineers is moderate. Might be 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon but do not offend\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat\n1 = radically violates\n\nLogging SDK is acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities.\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nNeed output format: echo id, then for each subscale give <subscale>_evidence and <subscale>. Probably JSON? The instruction says give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer. Might output as lines.\n\nI'll output:\n\nid: P1560\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\netc.\n\nMake one sentence evidence each.\n\nEnsure order listed: paradigm_relatedness, originality, effectiveness, applicability, implementability, acceptability\n\nProceed.\n\n",
