        "content": "{\"ratings\":[{\"id\":\"P1527\",\"originality_evidence\":\"Embedding compliance checks in CI/CD pipelines is a common DevOps practice for regulatory controls, not rare or ingenious.\",\"originality\":1,\"paradigm_relatedness_evidence\":\"The proposal adds pipeline gates and automated validation but still treats Article 12 as logging practice rather than changing what the lab researches.\",\"paradigm_relatedness\":2,\"effectiveness_evidence\":\"If implemented, mandatory log-schema and retention checks before promotion would ensure high-risk systems technically allow automatic logging as required.\",\"effectiveness\":4,\"applicability_evidence\":\"The gate directly addresses meeting Article 12 record-keeping for labs deciding how to comply with logging mandates.\",\"applicability\":4,\"implementability_evidence\":\"Adding automated schema and retention checks to existing CI/CD requires moderate engineering changes but is reasonably feasible with current tooling.\",\"implementability\":3,\"acceptability_evidence\":\"Integrating compliance verification into normal engineering workflow is a common, norm-conforming strategy that does not offend legal or business sensibilities.\",\"acceptability\":4}]}",
