dit is standard compliance. Paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged. So level 1.\n\nCheck definitions: paradigm_relatedness 4 = paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. 3 = paradigm stretching changes that relationship... 2 = slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 = paradigm preserving standard compliance.\n\nAudit is standard. So 1.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence (one sentence) first and then <subscale> (integer). Order listed: effectiveness, applicability, implementability, acceptability, originality, paradigm_relatedness\n\nProvide evidence sentences.\n\nEnsure one sentence each.\n\nReturn rating.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Could be lines.\n\nLet's produce clear output.\n\nMaybe:\nid: P2739\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 3\n...\n\nOk.\n\n",
